#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# not_element

#% text
# `not_element(x, domain)` is the negation of `element(x, domain)`: `true` when x is known not to be in the domain, `false` when it is known to be.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The domains are those of `element`: `integers`, `rationals`, `reals`, `complexes` and their signed parts such as `positive_reals`.

#% item
# When membership is not decided the call stays unevaluated.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
not_element(pi, integers)
#% output
#= true

#% cell
not_element(x, reals)
#% output
#= not_element(x, reals)

#% subsection
# Scope

#% cell
[not_element(2/3, integers), not_element(2/3, rationals), not_element(-1, positive_reals)]
#% output
#= [true, false, true]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `element`, `assuming`, `refine`
